FORM S-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: statutes-of-arithmetic.
FILED BY: the bundled canon.

OFF THE RECORD: Arithmetic helpers not provided by built-in operators.
OFF THE RECORD: Each office uses only its arguments and recursive
OFF THE RECORD: petitions. The offices are reentrant and do not leave
OFF THE RECORD: records behind in the case that incorporates this
OFF THE RECORD: statute.

THE OFFICE OF absolute-value, CONCERNING n.
    SHOULD n FALL SHORT OF 0, REMAND WITH 0 LESS n.
    REMAND WITH n.

THE OFFICE OF maximum, CONCERNING a AND b.
    SHOULD a EXCEED b, REMAND WITH a.
    REMAND WITH b.

THE OFFICE OF minimum, CONCERNING a AND b.
    SHOULD a FALL SHORT OF b, REMAND WITH a.
    REMAND WITH b.

THE OFFICE OF signum, CONCERNING n.
    SHOULD n EXCEED 0, REMAND WITH 1.
    SHOULD n FALL SHORT OF 0, REMAND WITH 0 LESS 1.
    REMAND WITH 0.

THE OFFICE OF power, CONCERNING base AND exponent.
    SHOULD exponent FALL SHORT OF 0, HOLD "a negative exponent asks for a fraction, and the Court keeps nothing finer than the penny" IN CONTEMPT.
    SHOULD exponent EQUAL 0, REMAND WITH 1.
    REMAND WITH base TIMES (THE FINDING OF power REGARDING base AND exponent LESS 1).

THE OFFICE OF greatest-common-divisor, CONCERNING a AND b.
    SHOULD b EQUAL 0, REMAND WITH THE FINDING OF absolute-value REGARDING a.
    REMAND WITH THE FINDING OF greatest-common-divisor REGARDING b AND a NOTWITHSTANDING b.
